      "slack_rationale": "Four window standard deviations, chosen empirically. Where a reference has replicas the choice can be checked against an independent run: leave one replica out, calibrate on the rest, score every window of the held-out one. Over the 39 references that allow it, four takes 37, 37 and 38 of them to zero observed rejections on the three checks. Thirty windows per fold bounds the true per-submission rejection rate at roughly one in ten, not at zero, and the same figure cannot be measured at all on the 61 single-replica references, whose bands are built inside one trajectory and are therefore narrower than a between-run band by a median factor of 1.21 and up to 2.84. The value applies to every task alike: demoting a check only where the evidence exists would penalise the references that carry more of it. Two window SD, the value measured on three PLpro tasks by cross-validation inside one trajectory, leaves a correct submission rejected 10 per cent of the time at the median and 70 at the worst.",
